## Important 1: sentenceCount regexes dropped the straight apostrophe (U+0027)
- Location: src/textstats.js:39 (TERMINATOR_PATTERN) and src/textstats.js:46 (endsWithAbbreviation opener strip).
- Issue: commit aef2cc6 restored the curly quotes but removed U+0027 from both character classes.
  Current line 39: /([.!?]+)(["”’)\]]*)(?=\s|$)/g      Plan (plan.md:305): /([.!?]+)(["'”’)\]]*)(?=\s|$)/g
  Current line 46: .replace(/^["“‘(\[]+/, '')           Plan (plan.md:311): .replace(/^["'“‘(\[]+/, '')
- Reproduced: sentenceCount("'Go.' Then left.") returns 1 (expected 2);
  sentenceCount("He met ('Dr. Wren) today.") returns 2 (expected 1).
- Recommendation: restore U+0027 in both classes exactly as plan.md shows (compare code points);
  add tests for both inputs in test/sentenceCount.test.js.

